# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE ON SYNTAX: .gitignore does NOT support inline comments. A trailing
# `# ...` becomes part of the pattern, so `!.env.example  # keep this` silently
# matches nothing and the file stays ignored. Every comment here is therefore
# on its own line. This is not a style preference — it is a correctness rule.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS - the most important lines in this file.
# An API key committed to a repo is scraped by bots within minutes, and
# rewriting git history to remove it is painful. Never relax these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
# ...but the template holds no real values and MUST be committed:
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# --- Databases -------------------------------------------------------------
# Local SQLite files. Each developer's data is their own; committing one would
# overwrite everyone else's.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Node / Next.js --------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
.vercel/
*.tsbuildinfo
# Regenerated by Next.js on every build:
next-env.d.ts

# --- Editors and OS --------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Logs ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
